## 1. The Big Idea

_This is the **Calibration Bench** poster. The hero is a **zeroing gauge**: one instrument face with the factory reference band ghosted (`POPULATION AVERAGE — NOT YOU`) and a freshly-struck personal zero mark (`YOUR ZERO — set while healthy`), stamped with the article's law: `YOU CANNOT MANAGE WHAT YOU HAVE NEVER MEASURED.` Around it, the full calibration pass: a five-step **sample-prep chain** (bad prep → false readings → wrong interventions, with the cranked-AI-against-fake-E2 fault as the worked example), a six-bay **instrument rack** of the baseline panel with each bay's headline marker called out and the hormone bay flagged as the most important, the **compensated sensor pairs** that solve the lifter's interference problem (creatinine→cystatin-C, AST/ALT→GGT), a **growth-signal interlock** (sweep cancer markers before GH/IGF-1 — growth signals grow whatever is already there), a **sealed archival sample** (semen analysis + freeze at >1 clinic — the one reading you can't take later), and an **inspection timetable** (home layer always-on + four blood checkpoints) stamped `EVERY 6–12 MONTHS = MONITORING IN NAME ONLY.` A Malaysia spec rail prices the whole pass in RM._ The poster is the metrology certificate the rest of the 15-article track assumes exists.

## 2. Visual Metaphor & Structure

A **pre-energization calibration bench** — the metrology station where every gauge gets zeroed to the specific machine before first power-up. Visual language: calibration certificates, zero-adjust screws, compensated sensor schematics, sample chain-of-custody tags, inspection timetables. Six functional zones plus a side rail:

- **Zone 1 — The Zeroing Gauge (hero).** One large instrument face. The factory reference band is printed but **ghosted/de-emphasized**, labeled `LAB REFERENCE RANGE — population average`. A bold, freshly-struck zero mark sits at the needle, labeled `YOUR ZERO — your healthy set-point`. A small zero-adjust screw is drawn being turned. Law plate under the face: `YOU CANNOT MANAGE WHAT YOU HAVE NEVER MEASURED.` Three output chips hang off the gauge (what a baseline buys): `① CATCHES DEALBREAKERS — some baselines say: don't.` (with a thin tie-line back to the 1.0 NO-GO rail) · `② YOUR REFERENCE POINT — "is this high?" only answers against you` · `③ FERTILITY, CAPTURED — the reading you can't take later`.
- **Zone 2 — The Sample-Prep Chain (chain-of-custody strip).** Five tagged steps drawn as a specimen-handling sequence: `HYDRATE 1–1.5 L` (dehydration fakes hematocrit · creatinine · electrolytes) → `FAST 10–12 h` → `DRAW 07:00–10:00` (hormones at circadian peak = comparable numbers) → `HOLD TRAINING 48–72 h` (training inflates CPK · AST · ALT) → `ABSTAIN 3 d` (semen analysis). At the strip's end, the fault chip that justifies it: `FALSE E2 READING → AI CRANKED AGAINST A NUMBER THAT WAS NEVER REAL. Bad prep doesn't just lie — it prescribes.`
- **Zone 3 — The Instrument Rack (the baseline panel, six bays).** A rack elevation, each bay a slim module with its headline marker enlarged and one teach-line: `BAY 1 · CBC — headline: HEMATOCRIT` (androgens stimulate RBC production; respect plate: `>52–54% → phlebotomy + hydration → Part 4.0`) · `BAY 2 · CARDIOVASCULAR CORE — headline: HDL + ApoB` (`where the cost shows first` — orals crush HDL; ApoB = particle count, the one extra worth buying; hs-CRP · homocysteine in small print) · `BAY 3 · KIDNEY — headline: CYSTATIN-C` · `BAY 4 · LIVER — headline: GGT` · `BAY 5 · HORMONES — THE MOST IMPORTANT BAY` (drawn slightly wider/brighter: `T total/free · SHBG >~20 nmol/L · E2 sensitive assay · LH/FSH — what the cycle suppresses · prolactin — the 19-nor tell · IGF-1 — the GH readout`; caption `your "after" is meaningless without a complete "before"`) · `BAY 6 · SUPPORT — thyroid · vit D/B12/zinc · electrolytes · heavy metals`.
- **Zone 3b — The Compensated Sensor Pairs (detail inset on the rack).** The lifter's interference problem as a two-channel schematic, drawn once and clearly: interference source `MUSCLE MASS + TRAINING` injects into the raw channels `CREATININE/eGFR` and `AST/ALT` (both flagged `READS FALSELY STRESSED IN LIFTERS`), each paired with its corrected channel `CYSTATIN-C — muscle-independent` and `GGT — liver-specific` with the decoder line `GGT normal + AST/ALT high = muscle, not liver.` Caption: `A LIFTER'S BODY JAMS THE STANDARD SENSORS — ORDER THE COMPENSATED PAIR.`
- **Zone 4 — The Growth-Signal Interlock.** A gate drawn across the input line labeled `GH · IGF-1 · GROWTH PEPTIDES`, held open only by a completed sweep: `CANCER-MARKER SWEEP REQUIRED FIRST.` The physics plate: `GROWTH SIGNALS DON'T CAUSE CANCER — THEY ACCELERATE WHAT'S ALREADY THERE.` A compact organ-map strip (prostate · liver · colorectal · pancreas · lung · stomach · testes · pituitary · thyroid ← AFP · PSA/f-PSA · CEA · CA 19-9 · β-HCG · NSE · hGH …) rendered as a small grid, not a table dump. Cadence chips: `EVERY ~3 YEARS` · `YEARLY if family history`. Pituitary caveat in fine print: `baseline GH/LH/FSH/prolactin very high before starting anything → investigate (imaging) first.`
- **Zone 5 — The Archival Sample (vault chip).** A small sealed-vault module: `SEMEN ANALYSIS — volume · count · concentration · motility · morphology` → `IF NORMAL: FREEZE. Multiple samples · MORE THAN ONE CLINIC.` Teach-line: `a verified backup of the system state, stored off-site, before you flash anything.` Tagged `NON-RETAKEABLE` — the only reading on the bench with an expiry.
- **Zone 6 — The Inspection Timetable (monitoring cadence).** Two layers drawn as a maintenance schedule. **Layer 1 · HOME, ALWAYS-ON:** `BP — several×/week, seated, same hour — the cheapest early-warning system you own` · `RHR — daily trend` · `WEIGHT — trend + water` (pointer chip: `the continuous film → Part 2.1`). **Layer 2 · BLOOD CHECKPOINTS:** four ticks on a cycle-time axis — `BASELINE (full panel)` → `MID-CYCLE wk 4–6 (hematocrit · lipids · E2 · prolactin if 19-nors · liver if orals · glucose if GH)` → `END / PRE-PCT (+ LH · FSH · T)` → `POST-PCT 4–8 wk (did the axis come back?)`. The mid-cycle tick is the emphasized one, with the danger plate: `INVISIBLE WITHOUT MID-CYCLE LABS: hematocrit at stroke territory · HDL near zero · 150/95 sitting quietly.` Stamp across the layer: `EVERY 6–12 MONTHS = MONITORING IN NAME ONLY.`
